WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.525 --> 00:00:17.248
Mrs. Lynde, an old friend of Marilla's, had come to Green Gables to visit and discuss the latest

2
00:00:17.288 --> 00:00:20.149
town "news," though most people called it gossip.

3
00:00:22.149 --> 00:00:25.891
"I've heard that you started an improvement society, Anne.

4
00:00:26.811 --> 00:00:27.611
Is it true?"

5
00:00:28.211 --> 00:00:28.751
asked Mrs.

6
00:00:28.811 --> 00:00:32.489
Lynde. "Not really," said Anne, flushing.

7
00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:35.191
"I was just talking it over with some friends.

8
00:00:35.991 --> 00:00:38.433
Many towns have improvement societies now."

9
00:00:38.453 --> 00:00:43.077
"It's not a good idea," said Mrs.

10
00:00:43.137 --> 00:00:46.879
Lynde. "People don't like being improved, Anne."

11
00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:51.863
"We're not improving the people," said Anne.

12
00:00:51.883 --> 00:00:54.525
"We want to make Avonlea prettier.

13
00:00:55.606 --> 00:00:58.748
For instance, we're thinking of painting the town hall."

14
00:01:00.328 --> 00:01:08.353
Mrs. Lynde was unconvinced, but soon the Avonlea Improvement Society was organized, with Gilbert Blythe as president, Fred

15
00:01:08.433 --> 00:01:13.636
Wright as vice-president, Anne Shirley as secretary, and Diana Barry as treasurer.

16
00:01:15.577 --> 00:01:22.001
The Improvement Society received some disapproval and a good deal of ridicule from Avonlea's older citizens.

17
00:01:23.402 --> 00:01:27.364
Mr. Wright said a better name for the Society would be the "Dating Club."

18
00:01:28.648 --> 00:01:33.330
Mr. Bell said that he might be willing to paint his barn, but there was no way he'd

19
00:01:33.370 --> 00:01:35.231
hang lace curtains in his stables.

20
00:01:36.572 --> 00:01:39.753
Despite these jokes the "Improvers" set to work.

21
00:01:41.374 --> 00:01:45.276
Anne and Diana walked along an Avonlea road, visiting each house.

22
00:01:46.376 --> 00:01:50.478
They were collecting donations for the Improvement Society to paint the town hall.

23
00:01:51.538 --> 00:01:55.000
Their first stop was the home of Catherine and Eliza Andrews.

24
00:01:56.520 --> 00:02:02.502
"If Catherine is here, we might get some money," said Diana, "but if Eliza is there, we won't."

25
00:02:03.682 --> 00:02:06.723
Eliza Andrews answered the door, looking very grim.

26
00:02:07.663 --> 00:02:11.104
As the girls explained their errand, Catherine came to the door.

27
00:02:11.884 --> 00:02:15.305
Eliza listened with a frown, but Catherine smiled.

28
00:02:15.325 --> 00:02:21.727
"I won't give any money for that hall, not a cent," said Eliza sourly.

29
00:02:21.747 --> 00:02:25.108
"It's just a place for young people to meet.

30
00:02:26.156 --> 00:02:27.597
Young people should stay at home.

31
00:02:28.137 --> 00:02:30.137
This world is getting worse every day!"

32
00:02:30.157 --> 00:02:33.098
"I think it's getting better!"

33
00:02:33.558 --> 00:02:34.879
said Catherine firmly.

34
00:02:36.259 --> 00:02:37.719
Eliza changed the subject.

35
00:02:37.739 --> 00:02:40.060
"How are Marilla's eyes, Anne?

36
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:41.381
Is she blind yet?"

37
00:02:43.001 --> 00:02:46.042
"Her eyes aren't any worse," Anne replied meekly.

38
00:02:47.482 --> 00:02:53.184
Anne and Diana left disappointed, but as they headed down the road a woman ran up behind them.

39
00:02:54.428 --> 00:02:57.190
It was Catherine Andrews with a dollar in her hand.

40
00:02:57.210 --> 00:03:01.034
"Good luck with the Improvement Society!"

41
00:03:01.474 --> 00:03:01.994
she said.

42
00:03:03.055 --> 00:03:04.116
The girls cheered up.

43
00:03:05.437 --> 00:03:06.958
Their next visit was to Mrs.

44
00:03:07.019 --> 00:03:12.423
Bell, who looked very healthy but spent a half an hour describing all her aches and pains.

45
00:03:13.304 --> 00:03:18.448
Mrs. Bell gave them money but said she couldn't donate next year because she would probably be in

46
00:03:18.508 --> 00:03:19.429
her grave by then.

47
00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.032
The worst reception was at the Fletchers'.

48
00:03:23.920 --> 00:03:28.422
Anne and Diana saw two faces in the window as they walked up to the door, but when

49
00:03:28.562 --> 00:03:30.343
Anne knocked, nobody answered.

50
00:03:31.724 --> 00:03:35.305
Eventually the Improvers raised enough money to paint the hall.

51
00:03:36.006 --> 00:03:38.667
They decided on dark green and asked Mr.

52
00:03:38.727 --> 00:03:42.088
Joshua Pye, an uncle of Anthony Pye, to paint it.

53
00:03:43.189 --> 00:03:47.391
They had to give the contract to a member of the Pye family, or else none of the

54
00:03:47.491 --> 00:03:49.792
four Pye families would donate any money.

55
00:03:51.272 --> 00:03:55.135
Mr. Roger Pye brought the hall paint home that night, and Mr.

56
00:03:55.195 --> 00:03:57.457
Joshua Pye began painting the next day.

57
00:03:58.437 --> 00:04:00.199
He was not disturbed in his task.

58
00:04:01.820 --> 00:04:07.024
The hall was so closely surrounded by a wood of fir trees that it was invisible to anyone

59
00:04:07.084 --> 00:04:08.465
not driving right by it.

60
00:04:09.506 --> 00:04:14.409
Mr. Joshua Pye finished his job Friday afternoon and went home to Carmody.

61
00:04:15.310 --> 00:04:16.371
Later Mrs.

62
00:04:16.451 --> 00:04:17.592
Lynde drove by the hall.

63
00:04:18.664 --> 00:04:22.187
She was curious to see what the hall looked like in its new coat of paint.

64
00:04:24.289 --> 00:04:24.729
When Mrs.

65
00:04:24.789 --> 00:04:31.194
Lynde rounded the curve and saw the brilliant blue town hall, she dropped the reins and said, "Good

66
00:04:31.295 --> 00:04:36.959
gracious!" She stared for a moment and then laughed hysterically.

67
00:04:40.802 --> 00:04:43.324
News of the mistake quickly spread through Avonlea.

68
00:04:43.344 --> 00:04:46.107
"Oh, it's simply dreadful!"

69
00:04:46.607 --> 00:04:47.388
Anne exclaimed.

70
00:04:48.852 --> 00:04:53.855
"I just can't believe Joshua Pye has gone and painted the hall blue instead of green.

71
00:04:55.356 --> 00:04:58.757
It's the blue that people use to paint carts and wheelbarrows.

72
00:04:59.998 --> 00:05:00.438
And Mrs.

73
00:05:00.558 --> 00:05:04.641
Lynde says it's the most hideous color for a building that she's ever seen."

74
00:05:04.661 --> 00:05:08.263
"How on earth could such a mistake have happened?"

75
00:05:08.723 --> 00:05:09.443
asked Diana.

76
00:05:10.464 --> 00:05:13.826
The blame for this disaster was eventually pinned on the Pyes.

77
00:05:15.086 --> 00:05:18.088
The shades of paint were selected from a numbered color card.

78
00:05:18.816 --> 00:05:24.017
The Improvers had chosen the color number 147 and had told Roger Pye.

79
00:05:25.018 --> 00:05:30.039
However, Roger had somehow bought color number 157 instead.

80
00:05:30.059 --> 00:05:37.781
"I must cry, even if I am almost 17 years old, Marilla," Anne later sobbed.

81
00:05:37.801 --> 00:05:43.403
"It is so embarrassing—people will think the Improvement Society is a joke.

82
00:05:44.163 --> 00:05:47.604
They'll never again listen to our ideas or give us donations."

83
00:05:49.433 --> 00:05:53.595
In life, however, things often turn out differently from how we expect.

84
00:05:55.176 --> 00:05:58.438
The Avonlea people did not laugh at the Improvement Society.

85
00:06:00.160 --> 00:06:04.843
They had donated money to have the town hall painted, and they were angry about the mistake.

86
00:06:05.803 --> 00:06:08.085
Public indignation centered on the Pyes.

87
00:06:09.105 --> 00:06:12.648
People felt that Joshua Pye should have realized it was the wrong color.

88
00:06:13.976 --> 00:06:19.081
Joshua Pye argued that he painted the hall the color he was given, and it wasn't his job

89
00:06:19.121 --> 00:06:21.983
to question the Improvement Society's taste in color.

90
00:06:23.565 --> 00:06:29.470
Despite Joshua Pye's arguments, the people of Avonlea still took the Improvement Society's side.

91
00:06:30.330 --> 00:06:36.276
People believed the Improvers had worked hard, and many of them took inspiration from the Society's example.

92
00:06:37.557 --> 00:06:41.764
Mr. Major Spencer said he would plant flowers around the town, and Mr.

93
00:06:41.804 --> 00:06:43.825
Bell decided to paint his old barn.

94
00:06:45.386 --> 00:06:47.967
Anne, however, was still upset about the town hall.

95
00:06:47.987 --> 00:06:52.649
"Never mind, Anne," Marilla consoled her.

96
00:06:52.669 --> 00:06:55.691
"Most paint fades uglier over time.

97
00:06:56.871 --> 00:06:59.732
But that blue started out as ugly as it can be.

98
00:07:00.473 --> 00:07:02.714
So it's bound to fade prettier."

99
00:07:03.394 --> 00:07:05.855
Anne smiled, but she was not convinced.
